# What never needs to reach a container build context.
#
# The Containerfile COPYs only the paths it needs, so this file changes nothing
# about the image -- it keeps the context from carrying a few hundred megabytes
# of release archives and installer payload on every build.

.git
.gitignore

# Build outputs and payloads: dist/ is release archives, installer/vendor holds
# a hand-fetched llama.cpp, installer/payload is the assembled tree.
dist/
installer/
/gobbonet
/gobbonet.exe

# Generated by stage-web.sh. The build runs that script itself; a stale copy
# from the host is exactly what generating it exists to avoid.
web/

# Windows launcher and setup half -- PowerShell, batch, hardware probe. None of
# it runs in the image.
*.ps1
*.bat

# Local state and secrets. Present in a working checkout, meaningless or
# dangerous in an image.
config.toml
perf.toml
.env
.gobbonet-secret
.gobbonet-state.json
.gobbonet-port
models/
*.gguf
logs/
*.log

# Docs.
*.md
LICENSE
